Speaker 1: . I want to talk to you today about
what I'm calling the nexus the intersection

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.390
of immoral and stupid.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:16.330
And when I hear the nexus of immoral and stupid,
I think about a handful of members of Congress.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.680
And on that list is Republican Matt Gates.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:25.730
Matt Gates is voting against capping insulin
prices to the end user.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.030
Now it's crazy to use the term end user.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.570
When we're talking about medicine, I agree
with you.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:38.040
It's also a crazy situation because we are
only talking about capping the price of insulin

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.719
for the end user.

00:00:39.719 --> 00:00:46.780
So late last week, the House of Representatives
passed a Democratic sponsored bill to cap

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:52.920
insulin at $35 a month for most Americans
in terms of their out of pocket.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.460
Now, of course, you know, and I know and anybody
who's dealt with health insurance knows these

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.220
things cost way more, but health insurance
will pay part of it.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.709
And then there's a discount and blah blah
blah blah blah.

00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:09.499
I know some of you were sick of this example,
but it's been at least six months since since

00:01:09.499 --> 00:01:14.010
I've made it an example when I had my infamous
appendectomy.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:19.039
You might remember that the sticker price
was thirty five grand.

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:21.229
Now that's what the hospital billed.

00:01:21.229 --> 00:01:26.609
My insurance, my insurance had said Sirs and
M&amp;Ms at the hospital.

00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:29.859
We know people sometimes have appendicitis.

00:01:29.859 --> 00:01:36.759
Will you contract with us for appendectomies
for I believe it was $11000.

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:43.600
So of the thirty something thousand that the
hospital wanted, my insurance said we are

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.950
OK with 11 and I had a $2000 deductible.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:54.729
So the $35000 appendectomy ended up being
2000 for me and my insurance made up that

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:55.799
other $9000.

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:58.960
Similarly, with insulin, you know there are
people now who pay over a thousand dollars

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.350
a month in the price, the actual price of
insulin.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:06.419
My SRP sticker price wouldn't even change
with this bill.

00:02:06.419 --> 00:02:12.080
But the point here is insulin guys insulin
$35 a month.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.080
Let's cap it.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.489
And Matt Gates says no.

00:02:14.489 --> 00:02:16.430
Why does Matt Gates say no?

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:19.049
Basically, because people should just lose
weight.

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:23.840
He wrongly thinks not that it would really
make a big difference, but he wrongly thinks

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.739
only overweight people need insulin.

00:02:26.739 --> 00:02:35.200
Matt Matt Gates saying quote While Democrat
posturing of H.R. 60 833 victimizes insulin

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:40.489
pays as people with an uncontrollable disease
that are being taken advantage of and need

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:47.219
Big Brother to throw them a raft, lifestyle
changes and mass would expeditiously lower

00:02:47.219 --> 00:02:53.400
demand and the subsequent prices of insulin
90 to 95 percent of people with diabetes have

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.220
type two, which can be prevented or delayed
with healthy lifestyle changes such as losing

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:00.840
weight, eating healthy food and being active.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.090
Arbitrary price controls are no substitute
for individual weight control.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:09.439
Since 2000, the number of diabetes cases in
the U.S. has nearly doubled.

00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:13.719
The demand for insulin has increased and the
requisite price increase has followed suit.

00:03:13.719 --> 00:03:18.209
In other words, the price of insulin increases
as waistlines increase.

00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:20.150
So yes, he's a prick.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.140
Yes, of course, but he's also ignorant.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:30.739
Aside from this being asinine and disgusting
and just horrible, it's not accurate.

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:37.639
Type one diabetes is managed by taking insulin
to control blood sugar.

00:03:37.639 --> 00:03:45.829
Type two diabetes in more ways than type one
is managed in other ways.

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:48.139
This means medication.

00:03:48.139 --> 00:03:49.819
This means exercise.

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:50.819
This means diet.

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:54.500
When I say medication, I mean a pill, not
insulin.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.500
People with type two.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:02.129
Diabetes sometimes are prescribed insulin,
but insulin is about type one diabetes.

00:04:02.129 --> 00:04:06.719
Insulin is for type one diabetes, who are
often perfectly fit.

00:04:06.719 --> 00:04:12.280
It is for type one diabetes for people who
are not overweight.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.870
And there's a couple of different things here,
and I don't even know where to start, to be

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:17.870
totally honest, guys.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:20.299
I mean, on the one hand.

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:26.949
Should absolutely no condition related to
our own actions be covered, because then we're

00:04:26.949 --> 00:04:32.690
saying we're not covering lung cancer, most
of which is related to cigaret smoking.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:38.569
We're not covering injuries that happen as
a result of what we might call extreme sports

00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:40.730
or risky activities.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:44.490
We're not covering COVID stays for people
who are unvaccinated.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:48.900
I mean, so first of all, is this is this idea
that, hey, listen, I want people to live as

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:53.230
healthy lifestyle as possible, but are we
really saying we shouldn't be covering costs

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:57.740
for people who have certain conditions because
of how those conditions develop?

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.930
That seems very, very dangerous.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:00.930
No.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:05.270
Now, as I've said before, people will say,
but David, sir, didn't you say that if we

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:14.250
have a full E.R. and you need to start putting
COVID patients on ventilators, it seems OK

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:21.620
as part of triaging limited resources to say
the vaccinated people get the ventilator first

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.970
because they're more likely to survive and
they're more likely to follow medical directions

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.140
as to their care.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:31.039
That is different than saying you're just
not covered if you have type two diabetes,

00:05:31.039 --> 00:05:32.330
so that's number one.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:38.110
Number two, you know, we've talked before
about obesity seen as basically a moral failing.

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:42.440
So putting aside that insulin is mostly for
type one and Matt Gates is talking about type

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:51.280
two, this idea that we can only see we should
only see obesity as a moral failing is is

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.280
wrong.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:57.630
At the same time, it should be OK to say that
in the United States, lack of nutritional

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:03.569
education leads people to eat persistently
unhealthy diets for their entire lives.

00:06:03.569 --> 00:06:05.539
And we've got to be able to talk about that
as well.

00:06:05.539 --> 00:06:11.470
But when we talk about obesity, we're talking
about sometimes diet, sometimes genetic factors,

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:14.020
sometimes underlying disease.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.229
There's a lot of different things.

00:06:15.229 --> 00:06:21.470
And again, seeing obesity as the big moral
failing also is extraordinarily myopic.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:25.990
So and the fat shaming and stuff like that
does not appear to work.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:30.949
Matt Gates is discussing insulin should be
cheap to the end user.

00:06:30.949 --> 00:06:35.550
Maybe we call them the end customer or whatever
the case may be, and he's vital for voting

00:06:35.550 --> 00:07:36.720
